From: pdx203 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: bridge: metal2vulkan patch 0032, landscape frames without a copy in and turn each

Carries bridge/patches/0032-rotated-framebuffer-carry-and-one-copy-back.patch, applied after 0031: a rotated (framebuffer-only) texture's image
carries across command buffers while no other encoder ended with it, so a landscape frame no longer copies the whole
plane in and turns it; and its copy back is one copy of the staged span (the rows' padding included) instead of one
region per row (2560 blits on Turnip). Landscape frames cost ~30 ms of GPU against ~3 ms in portrait.

